        "id": 39278,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-01T03:26:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Rabit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/48/5774_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Rabit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If I remember correctly, this came up during play testing and the answers to your two questions, BaloTheJester, are \"Yes\" and \"Yes\".  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=12\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Agreed. A trigger in the middle of AoE would could cause a newly-put-in-play target to also be hit, AND a card doing multiple attacks which is destroyed would forestall the attackes that haven't yet occured.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>As for changing which X cards are hit due to triggers or destroyed cards, the question is moot, as <em>which</em> targets will be hit is determined all at once before any targets are attacked.</p>",
